                x-ref="answer"
            >
                <div
                    class="text-sm faq-item-body text-gray-600"
                ><div class="text-option">&#8203;<span style="color:rgb(88, 87, 94)">Louisville Metro requires door-to-door solicitors to have a solicitor&rsquo;s license issued by the&nbsp;</span><span style="color:rgb(88, 87, 94)">License and Permits Division, 444 S. 5th Street, Suite 200, Louisville, KY 40202. (502) 574-3591.&nbsp;</span><span style="color:rgb(88, 87, 94)">The license is roughly the same size as a Kentucky driver&rsquo;s license. The license is issued to</span><br /><span style="color:rgb(88, 87, 94)">individuals, not companies; therefore, EACH solicitor is REQUIRED to have one. Unlicensed&nbsp;</span><span style="color:rgb(88, 87, 94)">solicitors should be reported to the police.</span></div></div>
            </div>
        </div>
