                style=" ;"
                :style="{height: height}"
                x-ref="answer"
            >
                <div
                    class="text-sm faq-item-body text-gray-600"
                ><div class="text-option">&#8203;The original developers of Hills and Dales created a dedicated public roads right of way which extends 30 feet from the center of the paved road into your yard. The City Commission maintains the paved portion of the right of way, and you are responsible for maintaining the portion of the right of way that extends into your yard.<br /><br />If the City of Hills and Dales and/or a utility company needs access to this easement for road or utility maintenance or construction or to address an unsafe condition, you may need to remove what you have planted or installed in the public roads right of way. You can check this public roads right of way and other easements on your property by looking at the survey of your lot.</div></div>
            </div>
        </div>
